# proto-file: googlesql/compliance/known_error.proto
# proto-message: KnownErrorFile
#
# Compliance tests the emulator is known to fail, on every platform; known_errors_linux.textproto and
# known_errors_macos.textproto list those that fail on one only. A statement that fails is listed by
# its name, under the reason it fails, so that any other statement that fails, or a listed one that
# fails in a worse mode, fails the test. Remove a statement once it passes: `just
# compliance-summary` names those that do.

# The emulator rejects what it does not support as unsupported, which clients can tell apart from
# BigQuery's behavior: any statement may fail as UNIMPLEMENTED. A wrong result, or an error where
# BigQuery succeeds, still fails the test.
known_errors {
  mode: ALLOW_UNIMPLEMENTED
  reason: "The emulator rejects what it does not support"
  label: ".*"
}

# Statements that fail, by reason.

